## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical CGO memory ownership, error mapping, and thread-safety in a real-world persistent storage scenario.

## Key Concepts
- CGO memory ownership and malloc/free semantics
- Error code translation to Go errors
- Thread-safety across CGO calls using a mutex
- Go interface design for Open/Put/Get/Close operations
- Disk-backed snapshots and atomic commits

## Code Example
